        },
        "Mz": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "Pa/s",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Vertical face-normal AIR-MASS flux (Pa/s) at each cell's LOWER edge, +ve UPWARD: Mz = -OMEGA (GEOS-FP OMEGA is dP/dt, +ve DOWNWARD). OMEGA is CELL-CENTRED in the archived files, so the edge value averages the two flanking cells, clamped at the walls. The values at ke=1 and ke=NLEV+1 are NEVER READ: facediv_lev_mass_nf_k1/_kN hardcode the no-flux wall to 0, which is what makes the 7-level slab closed at its ~906 hPa top. Replaces the Stage-B analytic profile.",
